    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-20597",
      "knowledge_point_id": "7294399b-b139-5ee6-824c-5e28e4fc49ff",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Already in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-2y-3z=0 \\\\  & y+2z=0 \\\\  & z=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix $M$ is already in row echelon form.\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=2 \\\\  & y=4 \\\\  & z=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have he solution $x=2$, $y=4$ and $z=-2.$ Or, in vector form $⟨2,4,-2⟩.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "⟨2,4,2⟩"
