      "math_academy_id": "q-10644",
      "knowledge_point_id": "95a32907-8304-5dfd-8759-9e91503445bf",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Not in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & 3x+4y-z=11 \\\\  & x+y=2 \\\\  & 2x+2y+z=-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -1 & 11 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -10\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
