    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-131627",
      "knowledge_point_id": "95a32907-8304-5dfd-8759-9e91503445bf",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Not in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x+3y+2z=-5 \\\\  & x+4y+2z=-2 \\\\  & -2x-6y-3z=8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form, and then solve the linear system.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -2 & -6 & -3 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -10 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x=-10 \\\\  & y=3 \\\\  & z=-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have the solution $x=-10$, $y=3$, and $z=-2.$ Or, in vector form, $⟨-10,3,-2⟩.$",
