    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-131620",
      "knowledge_point_id": "95a32907-8304-5dfd-8759-9e91503445bf",
      "knowledge_point": "Finding the Reduced Row Echelon Form of a 3x3 System That Is Not in Row Echelon Form",
      "problem": "Consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y+z=4 \\\\  & 3x-8y+5z=10 \\\\  & -2x+6y-z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard Gauss-Jordan method to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to reduced row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTransforming $M$ to reduced row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}-{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -23 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
